METHOD OF APPLICATION
Ÿ | Clean the surface by manual & mechanical means. Remove all the loose materials or previous work done make it free from
 | any type of contaminants like oil, sand, debris, etc.
Ÿ | Prime the surface with max. 20% water adding to Tru PU. Mix it till it becomes homogeneous, then apply by brush or roller
 | to the surface. The coverage will be approx. 80-90 sq ft per kg. The coverage will depend on the substrate conditions.
Ÿ | Tru PU should be applied undiluted directly by brush to obtain a continuous ﬁlm.
Ÿ | After self-priming, two more coats are required, wherein the second coat should be applied perpendicular to the ﬁrst coat
 | at an interval of 6-8 hrs. (Humidity present in the atmosphere may increase the time interval).
Ÿ | It must be protected from mechanical damage during construction or backﬁlling.
--- PAGE 2 ---
 | TRU PU
 | TECHNICAL DATA SHEET
 | VER NO. N.1
Ÿ | Any damage may be repaired by spot application
Ÿ | If a water ﬂood test is to be run, the membrane should cured for a minimum of 10 days.
Ÿ | Tru PU is resistant to frost but adhesion will be weak if it is applied to frosted substrates/surfaces.
Ÿ | Application should be avoided if substrate temperatures are below 5ºC or rain forecast. For any further technical
 | information required please contact the Trubuild technical services department.
LIMITATIONS
Ÿ | For priming, the product should be diluted with water (20% maximum by weight, i.e. 4 kg of water for 20 kg of TRU PU on
 | site to achieve a workable consistency).
Ÿ | Water ponding test shall be done only once the coating is fully cured for 10 days.
Ÿ | After full cure, this product will be slightly tacky, hence it is recommended to use a separation layer such as geotextile or PE
 | sheet, then cover with a protection screed.
Ÿ | Out gassing is a naturally occurring phenomenon of concrete that can produce pinholes in subsequently applied
 | coatings. The concrete must be carefully assessed for moisture content, air entrapment, and surface ﬁnish prior to any
 | coating work. Installing the coating either when the concrete temperature is falling or stable can reduce outgassing. It is
 | generally beneﬁcial, therefore, to apply the embedment coat in the late afternoon or evening
Ÿ | For optimum application, do not allow TRU PU liquid to be heated by direct sunlight or other heat sources.
Ÿ | Not suitable for permanent water immersion, hence not recommended for water-retaining structures such as RC tanks,
 | swimming pools, water features, etc.
Ÿ | The 1st coat and 2nd coat of TRU PU should be applied without any dilution
Ÿ | During the curing process, micro bubbles are formed. This is a product characteristic, which does not aﬀect the protective
 | properties. For this reason, it should be ensured that the material is not applied at excessive ﬁlm thicknesses in one layer as
 | excessive ﬁlm thickness may create bubbles.
Ÿ | The product can be applied by brush, roller or airless spray. Work well with a brush in diﬃcult areas. Apply subsequent
 | layers 24 hrs after the application of ﬁrst layer.
Ÿ | If TRU PU has been exposed to UV light, its colour will be changed to yellow slightly-without losing its physical properties
 | but ﬂow is possible due to temperature of sun light in open to sky condition.
Ÿ | It is recommended to use a reinforced coating system with 45 gsm ﬂeece or ﬁbre net specially on the joints/corners etc to
 | increase its tensile property, however, the performance of the standard coating system is also excellent
Ÿ | A screed needs to be laid on the ﬁnished system.
Ÿ | Avoid coating in afternoon as it may lead to bubble formation.
Ÿ | RCC should be fully cured and in a sound condition.
